      "writtenOn": "2026-08-05T10:56:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The intent here is narrow: prevent remote (LDAP/AD) users from disabling the LDAP/AD service via ServiceEnabled\u003dfalse, which would invalidate their own session and lock out all remote users.\n\nIf we move this check upstream by stripping ConfigureManager in isUserPrivileged(), it blocks all PATCH /redfish/v1/AccountService operations for remote users, not just ServiceEnabled.\nThat seems too broad.\n\nDo you have any preferred approach to handle this within the abstraction boundary you described?",
      "parentUuid": "99904c7a_c4e6d01e",
